Z||000003||Tigger||10-11-2000||02:53 PM||||9" wides are pretty wide for a Fiero, likely they'll stick out if they are going to fit.  <P>I'd be concerned with the clearance between the tire and rear strut and the shock in the front.  I'd imagine you'd build some upper body strength using them on the fronts.  These RWD offset?.  Can't beat the deal tho.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-11-2000||03:49 PM||||depending on their offest.. but they are probly gunna stick out.. are you sure thier bolt pattern is correct? a lot of time a 14x9 will be for a like a 265(+)-60- on a regal/cutlass/chevelle which have 5x114.3 bolt pattern in stead of our 5x100. ||||reg||1
